  *   g survey          state of the GPU clock branches in the GCC and, only if that is safe, of the gpucc
+ *   g g1              G1: power the CX domain and the GMU clocks, then read the GMU
  *   g r ADDR [N]      read N 32-bit words (default 1, at most 16) at the physical address ADDR (hex)
  * Windows: GCC 0x100000..0x1fffff always; gpucc 0x2c90000..0x2c98fff only while gcc_gpu_cfg_ahb_clk is running (reading
- * it with that clock off would hang the bus). Nothing else is allowed yet. Offsets and bits come from the Linux
+ * it with that clock off would hang the bus); the GMU 0x2c6a000..0x2c8ffff only once G1 has left it readable. Offsets and bits come from the Linux
  * drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8150.c and gpucc-sm8150.c; the base of the gpucc is the one of cepheus.dts.
  */
 #if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_CEPHEUS)
 #include <sys/param.h>
 #include <sys/systm.h>
 #include <sys/errno.h>
+#include <kern/clock.h>
